-- title:
--   Level automorphism moves toric ℓ_g-torsion coordinates by c↦ c^{γ₀₀}
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q\ell_g$-th root of unity $\xi$, together with a ring map $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell_g)}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the unit reduction `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`, with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and let $\tau$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q (ξ ^ ℓg) q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`: for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\neq 0$, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the quotient of the images of $p_f$ and $p_g$ in $L((\mathsf q))$, and every ring map $\iota':L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota'(\xi^{\ell_g})=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the series $\iota'(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals that of $f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\rho=\begin{pmatrix}\rho_{00}&\rho_{01}/q\\ q\rho_{10}&\rho_{11}\end{pmatrix}$. Write $(x_d,y_d)=$ [`ModularCurve.tateToricPoint L q d`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelPCusps.html#L20) for the explicit pair of Laurent series attached to a unit $d$ of $L$ (the coordinates of the toric point $d$ on the Tate curve of parameter $\mathsf q^{q}$), and put $\zeta=\xi^q$, a primitive $\ell_g$-th root of unity, viewed as a unit. Assume given a Weierstrass variable change $C_0$ over $L((\mathsf q))$ with $u\,(2x_\zeta+1/6)=2y_\zeta+x_\zeta$, $r=-1/12$, $s=-1/2$, $t=1/24$ (constants via `HahnSeries.C`), and a unit $\mu$ of $K$ with $\mu\,(2y_{\zeta^{\gamma_{00}}}+x_{\zeta^{\gamma_{00}}})\cdot 2(x_\zeta+1/12)=(2y_\zeta+x_\zeta)\cdot 2(x_{\zeta^{\gamma_{00}}}+1/12)$ in $L((\mathsf q))$. Finally let $c\in L^\times$ satisfy $c^{\ell_g}=1$, $c\neq 1$, and let $X,Y,X',Y'\in K$ have Laurent series $u^{-2}(x_c-r)$, $u^{-3}(y_c-s(x_c-r)-t)$ and the same expressions with $c$ replaced by $c^{\gamma_{00}}$. Then $\tau X=\mu^2X'$ and $\tau Y=\mu^3Y'$.
--
--   This is the toric counterpart of the transport of cusp coordinates: the $K$-rational points obtained by applying the variable change $C_0$ to the toric $\ell_g$-torsion points of the Tate curve with parameter $\mathsf q^{q}$ are permuted by the level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ according to the diamond action $c\mapsto c^{\gamma_{00}}$, up to the unit $\mu$ recording the change of model. It feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.toPoint_levelAut_eq_zsmul_toPoint_of_map_eq_tateToricPoint_rigidDataH1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.toPoint_levelAut_eq_zsmul_toPoint_of_map_eq_tateToricPoint_rigidDataH1Pow), and rests on the existence statements for the modular forms whose quotients read the toric coordinates together with their behaviour under $\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_Diamond_levelAut_apply_eq_unit_pow_mul_of_coe_eq_tateToricPoint_variableChange.lean

